#
# Give the bridge a floor on each client's throughput. The bridge
# serves one request at a time, and patch 11's idle deadline sheds a
# client that goes silent but not one that trickles: a client moving a
# few bytes a second held signing for everyone for as long as its
# payload took (#31). The client's buffer now measures its throughput
# over time spent waiting on the client alone, never on the server, and
# sheds a client below 4 KiB/s over its most recent 60 s of it. The
# inner stream, relayed on the raw sockets past that floor, is bounded
# as a whole instead. See patches/README.md.
#
